{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse","id":397162,"title":"Speculation on the Lunar Curse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-07T21:24:08-08:00","id":397162,"title":"Speculation on the Lunar Curse?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar thematics will be more tightly focused on the dualism of a &quot;good&quot; person who has a monster inside, or a monster who has a good person inside. Rage, transformation, and shapeshifting will be much more strongly evinced in their narrative and their mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cromage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of &quot;dualism&quot; but I'm not so keen on the &quot;human vs monster&quot; and have actually seen that more in the province of (gasp!) other splats (don't kill me). I like the idea of Lunars being champions of two worlds--exiles, outsiders, emigrants, and wanderers--and having to either choose one world or another or somehow trying to reconcile them.<br /> <br /> ETA: More importantly I always hated chimerism and its tendency to drag Lunars into really dumb places. Maybe 3e will make it not suck.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human vs. monster isn't on the schedule. I'm not turning Lunars into a werewolf story.<br /> <br /> Chimeraism is going to be way different in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miss Maddy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent is the 'frenzy' aspect of the Lunar Exalted going to tied to all of this? Will Lunars be more emotional or moody? Will the Full Moon give limit? Will Lunar Limit breaks involve largely animal-themed expressions of primal emotion?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frenzy aspects are choice driven, not the default state of all Lunars. Full Moon insanity is getting tossed entirely out. Lunar Limit Breaks are undetermined, but are likely to change from what they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the above exchanges, I'm assuming that the Great Curse of the Lunar Exalted is not going to grant them a &quot;Man versus the Animal Within / Inner Monster&quot; narrative that reflects the Alchemical Host's &quot;man versus machine&quot; narrative (Clarity).<br /> <br /> Not having a Great Curse that drives the Lunars to fits of animal behavior also helps distinguish them from the Solar Exalted, who do have an &quot;inner monster&quot; struggle because their Great Curse drives them to fits of great passion (or fits of terrible dispassion).<br /> <br /> Still, what does that leave? Identity disassociation? Ie: Multiple personality disorder?<br /> <br /> <br /> Note that the inner struggle highlighted by their Great Curse may very well be completely distinct from their other inner struggle, which seems to center around their old but strong association with the Solar Exalted and how the disappearance of the Solars left the Lunar Exalted without a place in the world. The Lunar struggle to find a new purpose may be their reflection of Sidereal Arcane Fate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, to clarify the very first quotation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not big on the concept of dualism like this [between human and monster] in general, it seems to imply that there is some sort of necessary conflict between being a &quot;monster&quot; and a &quot;good person&quot; that require the two to be somehow separate.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely true, and largely phrased that way because if we had simply said &quot;Luna Exalts people who are monsters on the inside or the outside&quot; a lot of people would assume that we meant Lunars are Dexter, which, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T21:26:18-08:00","id":397187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103367#post103367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those topics where I feel like it will be vastly easier to speculate once the corebook is out. There are two big lacunae in the way of guesses: we don't know what Lunars look like in Third Edition, and we don't know what the Solar Curse looks like in Third Edition. The dev comments on these two subjects have been interesting, but they're pretty thin grounds for extrapolation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, discussion will certainly be made easier after the corebook is out. But it's not impossible, either.<br /> <br /> We know that Solars are meant to evoke the greatest of Greek heroes, including their fits of excessive passion and other overreactions. We don't know the precise mechanical form this will take, but we know the character behind the mechanics and the inspiration behind that character.<br /> <br /> I just want to see if we can guess at the character and inspiration behind the Lunar Curse.<br /> <br /> Solars have to struggle against going overboard in anything they do, especially when their power is more than enough to take them exactly that far. Abyssals have to struggle against their fate to kill the world by inches (and miles). Alchemicals have to struggle against losing touch with humanity; Liminals might need to struggle in order to get in touch with humanity in the first place. Sidereals struggle to remain open-minded despite being in a position to &quot;know it all, and know it better than you&quot;.<br /> <br /> But against what does a shapeshifter tend to struggle, when you eliminate &quot;his own shapeshifting&quot; and &quot;the light of the full moon&quot; and &quot;losing his humanity in the face of the beast within&quot;?<br /> <br /> And make no mistake, the Lunar Curse isn't going to do something as stupid as punish Lunar players for turning into animals, because turning into animals is the <i>point</i> of playing the Lunars in the first place. If anything, it would be more appropriate for the Lunar Curse to act up when they <i>don't</i> shapeshift.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Curse will also not involve becoming more like the animals they turn into, because I quoted John Morke in the very first post, and he said he's not turning the Lunars into a werewolf &quot;man against inner monster&quot; story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103122#post103122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Jekyll and Hyde isn't on the table, perhaps Ratkin Rapture is. They were &quot;Gnosis frenzies&quot; that imparted distorted visions and premonitions when the rat was too much in tune with the spirit world. It included a number of effects that would be similar to being delusional, paranoid, etc., in addition to more mystical consequences like tuning out the world of matter and seeing only the spiritual landscape of the world.<br /> <br /> Going off of that last point, it might end up changing perceptions in a matter similar to the protagonist of Saya no Uta, who sees (and hears, and smells and otherwise perceives) humans as horrible, monstrous creatures and vice versa. The trailer for Oculus also comes to mind, but it's painful like that episode of Clone High where Abe's mouth keeps getting cut up, so beware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying Lunars more closely to the immaterial side of Creation <i>does </i>make sense, since the developers are drawing more inspiration from the Garou and the sources that inspired the Garou.<br /> <br /> Hmm. You've seen the <i>Karas </i>movie, right Saur Ops? Perhaps the Lunar Exalted have a similarly special relationship with the immaterial side of Creation, and all of the spirits that live there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103477#post103477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the inner struggle of the Lunar might not be a conflict, but rather a side of them that leaves them with a fairly powerful passion for the taboo or the extreme, something that can carry their reason along with it, and that many will allow it to*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting carried away by passion is what the Lunar Limit Break already did, and that didn't work because it was just copying the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that struggling to avoid wild flights of abandon and excess makes sense for ANY non-Solar Exalted except for the Terrestrial Exalted, who in some ways are &quot;the Solar Exalted, writ smaller&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> their manifestation of the Curse is something else... Maybe at one time it was being too heavily devoted to and dependent on the Solars, and then informed their evolution through the Second Age along lines of &quot;let's become the monsters everybody is saying we are&quot;...<br /> <br /> Hmm, the natural state of Lunars being highly individual, to the point of needing certain restraints based on their context within relationships to others, with their Great Curse as a force to make them <i>too much</i> what other people might observe them as being, rather than being themselves... </div> </div> </div>A curse of meeting and exceeding people's expectations of them might be very interesting, indeed. Certainly, it would introduce a powerful element to their other struggle, which is to find a new place and purpose in the world.<br /> <br /> It's hard to find yourself if you're constantly struggling to avoid becoming what other people think you should be.<br /> <br /> (It would also be another enormous, ironic allusion to how the player base has been treating the Lunar Exalted since their first splatbook was released.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/103039-what-is-the-inner-struggle-curse-for-the-lunar-exalted?p=103507#post103507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change of identity isn't really something you can enforce and model mechanically though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is. For a given value of &quot;identity&quot;. Or maybe, &quot;some parts of your identity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Intimacies (Ties and Principles) are important parts of a character's identity with mechanial representations.<br /> <br /> A Curse that targets the Lunar's identity might erode a particular Intimacy each time he acts against it, or the Curse might building a new Intimacy every time he acts in favor of it, or perhaps the Curse starts to change the emotion context of his lesser Intimacies every time he acts against (or in favor of) his stronger Intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T21:35:22-08:00","id":397189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397187#post397187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tying Lunars more closely to the immaterial side of Creation <i>does </i>make sense, since the developers are drawing more inspiration from the Garou and the sources that inspired the Garou.<br /> <br /> Hmm. You've seen the <i>Karas </i>movie, right Saur Ops? Perhaps the Lunar Exalted have a similarly special relationship with the immaterial side of Creation, and all of the spirits that live there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still no, but reading the article on it makes it sound like it's a huge mishmash of everything with cities as entities unto themselves, so it's hard to tell. Still think everything in it might be better for other Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T21:57:16-08:00","id":397194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397187#post397187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And make no mistake, the Lunar Curse isn't going to do something as stupid as punish Lunar players for turning into animals, because turning into animals is the <i>point</i> of playing the Lunars in the first place. If anything, it would be more appropriate for the Lunar Curse to act up when they <i>don't</i> shapeshift.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a limit which increases by suddenly taking a strange form, or relying on the same transformation time and time again. Like in <i>&quot;A Wizard of Earthsea&quot;</i> or <i>&quot;Howl's Moving Castle&quot;</i> where there is a risk of losing yourself in a transformation if you turn to it unprepared, or simply too many times. I'm not sure what would specifically drive the limit up, but the limit break at the end could involve you losing yourself in the intimacies and motivations of the form you took that finally pushed you over the edge into limit break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:14:07-08:00","id":397198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397194#post397194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a limit which increases by suddenly taking a strange form</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a false/stolen form?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or relying on the same transformation time and time again. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's <i>one </i>idea for encouraging Lunar players to constantly change it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:14:23-08:00","id":397200,"title":"","content":"You turn into a 2E lunar and become interested in playing SIM City while being totally incapable of meaningfully contributing to fights against opponents that matter without dying in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:21:13-08:00","id":397205,"title":"","content":"The <i>real</i> curse Lunars suffer through is the Curse of the Rabid Fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T23:35:52-08:00","id":397240,"title":"","content":"Sach, none of that has anything to do with the Lunar Curse.<br /> <br /> This is the second time I have attempted this thread. The first time was completely derailed by people talking about what Lunar shapeshifting should and shouldn't do.<br /> <br /> Please don't make that happen for me a second time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T23:59:11-08:00","id":397251,"title":"","content":"You shift into your spirit shape and have to spend X number of days living as that animal/creature would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T03:11:44-08:00","id":397328,"title":"","content":"Whatever it is. I hope it's sweeping and tragic.<br /> <br /> The idea of the Great Curse as laid out in the original, first form of the Exalted Core is solid IMO (please let's not start that again). It is intended as a spur to emulating epic tragedy, or as human passion and flaws to struggle against (with triumph possible).<br /> <br /> When it becomes an idea that each form of Exalt has a tendency to its own particular and random form of idiocy or mental illness or source of inconvenience, no matter whether those are anything to do with actual epic tragedy, when they just become Sanity level 0 stuff, then it becomes a farce.<br /> <br /> So I would only say for Lunars, whatever the Great Curse is for them, please, please, please put the aim of genre before finding some unique curse that it is reasoned that they could suffer from their inner nature, but which fails to generate interesting, emotionally touching and grand stories and explore human character. Start from what stories and character we want, then work backwards to try and fit it into what the Lunars are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T03:11:58-08:00","id":397329,"title":"","content":"What the hell is going on with the first two posts of this thread? :S","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T07:09:13-08:00","id":397523,"title":"","content":"I don't really see why Lunar Limit (Break) needs to be thematically different from the triggers for and expression of Solar Limit (Break). Both are arising from the same place of &quot;epic hero stress valve release.&quot; In this particular case I don't see cross-splat homogeneity as an inherently Bad Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T07:15:18-08:00","id":397525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397205#post397205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>real</i> curse Lunars suffer through is the Curse of the Rabid Fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we please not? There's a time and a place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T09:49:20-08:00","id":397694,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397251#post397251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You shift into your spirit shape and have to spend X number of days living as that animal/creature would.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>I'm not turning Lunars into a werewolf story.</b></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Look, I know that's exactly the first thing everyone comes up with, which is why I was VERY CLEAR in the original post that John had murdered the idea in the cradle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Human versus monster isn't on the schedule.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397523#post397523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why Lunar Limit (Break) needs to be thematically different from the triggers for and expression of Solar Limit (Break). Both are arising from the same place of &quot;epic hero stress valve release.&quot; In this particular case I don't see cross-splat homogeneity as an inherently Bad Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Limit Breaks are undetermined, but are likely to change from what they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary developer of the game seems to think it's a Bad Thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can we please move on to addressing the possibilities that <i>weren't </i>eliminated in the original post by Word of Morke?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-08-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:25:07-08:00","id":397746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397198#post397198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like a false/stolen form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, or if they have like &quot;Oh Shit Button&quot; charms that allow them to make a sudden situational change that they really shouldn't be able to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397198#post397198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's <i>one </i>idea for encouraging Lunar players to constantly change it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't want it to be a punishment for using your staple charms, but I could see putting a limit increase on some animal emulation charms if you use them more than once in a day or maybe a week or month. On to the end of those charms I would pin a little statement of what break causes if that charm is the one that pushes you into limit break.<br /> <br /> So lets say you have a charm called &quot;Insight of the Owlkin&quot; which lets you hear lies in the slightest wavering of a targets words, like an Owl hears the slightest crunch of snow as a mouse passes below supposedly hidden. If you use the charm more than once in a day you would gain a dot of Limit, if that dot puts you into Limit Break you enter the state described at the end of the charm: Obsession of the Owlkin: You see the signs of weakness and flaws all around you and are compelled to hunt the weak whether it be through direct violence or more surreptitious attacks on their credibility and influence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:32:27-08:00","id":397754,"title":"","content":"To lead off, I'd like to note I pretty much completely agree with Gayo: I genuinely don't feel that we know nearly enough about EX3 Lunars or EX3 Limit Break to make much headway here. That said, speculation can still lead to interesting places, so here goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397187#post397187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A curse of meeting and exceeding people's expectations of them might be very interesting, indeed. Certainly, it would introduce a powerful element to their other struggle, which is to find a new place and purpose in the world.<br /> <br /> It's hard to find yourself if you're constantly struggling to avoid becoming what other people think you should be.<br /> <br /> (It would also be another enormous, ironic allusion to how the player base has been treating the Lunar Exalted since their first splatbook was released.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of what I've thought most likely for a while. It also has the interesting quality that, if you have successfully found an identity and convinced basically everyone of it, it becomes a self-reinforcing thing. Though that <i>does</i> make it tricky to change one's identity.<br /> <br /> As a minor side-note, it raises a chicken-and-egg consideration on Immaculate teachings of the Lunar Anathema: were they simply accurate descriptions of how Lunars behaved, or were they originally propaganda pieces that Lunars (perhaps with the Curse's influence) decided to make into self-fulfilling prophecies? I mean, the answer is probably, &quot;Some of both,&quot; and now &quot;what the teachings say&quot; and &quot;how Lunars appear to act&quot; are just really self-reinforcing things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure it is. For a given value of &quot;identity&quot;. Or maybe, &quot;some parts of your identity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Intimacies (Ties and Principles) are important parts of a character's identity with mechanial representations.<br /> <br /> A Curse that targets the Lunar's identity might erode a particular Intimacy each time he acts against it, or the Curse might building a new Intimacy every time he acts in favor of it, or perhaps the Curse starts to change the emotion context of his lesser Intimacies every time he acts against (or in favor of) his stronger Intimacies. </div> </div> </div>I wonder to what degree it goes, though; at least on the surface, it seems like it would interact in an... interesting fashion with their shapeshifting. If you are disguising yourself as someone, among the unexamined expectations onlookers are going to have is that you are going to behave and think like this individual. The same goes for a Lunar in animal form: people expect an animal to think and behave like the animal they think she is. Should those expectations factor in when the Great Curse comes a'calling?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the mechanical form of Limit Break might then involve degrading/repressing Intimacies that aren't appropriate for those expectations, and adding/bolstering Intimacies that are. If a Lunar eats the heart of a wicked prince with the ultimate intent of reforming the kingdom with that shape, should he work too slowly, the lingering negative expectations of that prince may give the Lunar unwanted Intimacies or otherwise make it harder to do what he originally wanted. A Lunar playing the part of a beloved pet on a really long-term reconnaissance or &quot;sleeper agent&quot; operation may likewise end up with unwanted desires or otherwise lose bits of himself.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it should quite go so far, though. Maybe in very extreme cases (like with Lilith...?), as there are some interesting stories with precedent (Ged from a Wizard of Earthsea, as mentioned). It's something I'd find neat, but there's a certain wariness most people might have of being penalized for using one's powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397523#post397523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why Lunar Limit (Break) needs to be thematically different from the triggers for and expression of Solar Limit (Break). Both are arising from the same place of &quot;epic hero stress valve release.&quot; In this particular case I don't see cross-splat homogeneity as an inherently Bad Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Ghosthead was correct up above: what a given splat's Limit Break should be is <i>really</i> dependent on the sorts of stories that splat is meant to tell. I'm not opposed to the Lunar Limit Break being similar or identical to the Solar one if that facet of their experience is supposed to be similar, and I am opposed if it's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397329#post397329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell is going on with the first two posts of this thread? :S</div> </div> </div> </div>It bewildered me greatly last night. I just threw up my hands and said, &quot;Dammit. Forums, congratulations. Every time I think you've run out of ways to screw with presentation, you go out and prove you can still top yourself.&quot;* Then I noticed the timestamp and that the second post's quotes were from Sunder's last thread on this topic. So I presume he found them relevant to touch upon here and/or had missed them last time, but didn't want to dredge up the old thread itself to tackle them.<br /> <br /> * Not to pigeonhole activity, but there is a chance Sach <i>may</i> do something with this sentence. This is a chance I am willing to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:34:56-08:00","id":397774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397240#post397240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sach, none of that has anything to do with the Lunar Curse.<br /> <br /> This is the second time I have attempted this thread. The first time was completely derailed by people talking about what Lunar shapeshifting should and shouldn't do.<br /> <br /> Please don't make that happen for me a second time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I could see how you could translate a curse out of that Idea, if there are charms that make a Lunar &quot;of a place&quot; or &quot;of an essence&quot; using those charms could push you down a track of being permanently tied to those places. A lunar who specifically becomes of the shadowlands could find it harder and harder to be of some other place, at least until they have a shadowlands inspired break and get sent far enough back down the limit track to re-specialize if they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 02-08-2015, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:39:29-08:00","id":397777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397329#post397329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell is going on with the first two posts of this thread? :S</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397754#post397754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bewildered me greatly last night. I just threw up my hands and said, &quot;Dammit. Forums, congratulations. Every time I think you've run out of ways to screw with presentation, you go out and prove you can still top yourself.&quot;* Then I noticed the timestamp and that the second post's quotes were from Sunder's last thread on this topic. So I presume he found them relevant to touch upon here and/or had missed them last time, but didn't want to dredge up the old thread itself to tackle them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first time and this second time, the original post is filled with quotes from the &quot;What We Know&quot; Wiki in regards to Lunars and what stories they are and are NOT meant to tell, so as to inform a discussion about what form their Curse would take.<br /> <br /> The first thread was almost immediately derailed and bogged down with a debate about what Lunar shapeshifting should and shouldn't be able to do. It was so bad that I couldn't just bump the thread and hope for people to read only the original and later posts; they would undoubtably read the derail and respond chiefly to the derail.<br /> <br /> So I reposted the first post under a different title, then took the most relevant bits from the first thread and posted them second in a desperate effort to point the discussion where I wanted it to go.<br /> <br /> Look at how Sach jumped (seemed to jump?) directly to that derail despite my efforts! I assure you, it would have been worse with a simple bump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T10:55:04-08:00","id":397785,"title":"","content":"Oh, no, I'm not questioning your actions; that sums up what I thought were your reasons. I just didn't initially understand what was going on (possibly since I was exhausted, and deep asleep within 10 minutes of having read it), and attributed it to there <i>actually</i> being more posts in this thread (the ones to which you were responding) that the forum had decided to hide from me. I now see the full picture and attribute it to logical action on your part.<br /> <br /> Anyway! All is well and I don't think this tangent needs any more attention. ... He says, having extended it by another post. ^_^o Ah well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:08:48-08:00","id":397796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397785#post397785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, no, I'm not questioning your actions</div> </div> </div> </div>But I <i>am</i> confirming your hypothesis, and directly answering Levi's question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:19:12-08:00","id":397820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies again!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no. It's my fault for not thoroughly reading your post. Which I still haven't taken the time to do, and which I can't do before I leave for work in a few minutes.<br /> <br /> But I will!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:29:26-08:00","id":397829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies again! But as turkeygiant said, I only meant to &quot;translate a curse out of the idea&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not focused on shapeshifting. Not focused on charms. My only interest in those powers was to validate the &quot;worldwalker&quot; archetype as equally valid as compared to the &quot;animal inspired Great Curse&quot; stuff. You also mentioned Alchemical Clarity, so I naturally wondered &quot;would Lunars experience something similar, if they could somehow tie themselves to Autochtonia?&quot; followed with &quot;what other alien mindsets will slowly creep up on Lunars? would one in the Underworld get something like Whispers? what would it be like in Yu shan or Malfeas?&quot;<br /> <br /> You guys are focusing on &quot;madness tied to Intimacies&quot; - and that's awesome, I'll leave you to it.<br /> <br /> I was just injecting &quot;madness tied to loss or change of self-identity&quot; is also valid. It's also closer to the madness of Chimera, without turning you into an NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I especially like the idea of Lunars having the potential to get lost in the identity of their transformation because it sets them apart from Sidereal transformations. A resplendent destiny isn't real, It's always just one poke or prod away from unraveling, but when a Lunar transforms into something or someone else they are truly becoming that thing, so it would be fitting if they have the opposite problem of the transformation being difficult to shed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T11:32:54-08:00","id":397832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397829#post397829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I especially like the idea of Lunars having the potential to get lost in the identity of their transformation because it sets them apart from Sidereal transformations. A resplendent destiny isn't real, It's always just one poke or prod away from unraveling, but when a Lunar transforms into something or someone else they are truly becoming that thing, so it would be fitting if they have the opposite problem of the transformation being difficult to shed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care for the notion that your native splat power is also the source of your epic weakness. I mean sure, it logically makes sense, I just don't care for tying negative mechanics to a power you want to incentivize use of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:07:56-08:00","id":397878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys are focusing on &quot;madness tied to Intimacies&quot; - and that's awesome, I'll leave you to it.<br /> <br /> I was just injecting &quot;madness tied to loss or change of self-identity&quot; is also valid. It's also closer to the madness of Chimera, without turning you into an NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>We may be operating from different understandings of what EX3 Intimacies are going to be. I myself expect one's Intimacies to be strong statements about and facets of a character's self and identity. Whatever the new Intimacies system is evidently obviates Motivation and the Virtues, and it's been said they can have a fairly sizable impact. Our arguments may not be all that far apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397832#post397832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really care for the notion that your native splat power is also the source of your epic weakness. I mean sure, it logically makes sense, I just don't care for tying negative mechanics to a power you want to incentivize use of.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me on a topic like this, execution counts for a lot. Obviously, Pattern Spider Roulette is a shining example of how <i>not</i> to do this, but I think it's very possible to incentivize the use of powers while also maybe requiring some setup or carrying some cost or risk. I think of Holden's remarks recently:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden on Volcano Cutter's final Evocation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[All Creation Turns to Ash] does\u2026 not quite what it says on the tin, but change the name to \u201cHey, Where\u2019d Nighthammer District Go?\u201d and you\u2019re pretty close.<br /> <br /> But if you don\u2019t have fundamental combat skills, you will never, ever, ever manage to actually perform the necessary set-up for that Evocation\u2019s deployment, much less use it without killing yourself and your whole Circle in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think negatives are problematic unless they come off as overly punitive or outweigh the advantages -- or suck out a lot of the fun -- of the power in the first place. It also helps, as Holden notes in the second sentence, if the negatives are something with which you can meaningfully interact. Like, given the destructive potential of ACTtA, maybe it carries the risk of being caught up in the danger zone you've just unleashed, which you can help mitigate by being adept at getting the hell out of there. Likewise, if this has any bearing on shapeshifting, I expect it certainly wouldn't be a constant risk of use, and that there may be steps a Lunar can take to help mitigate what risks there are (or that a Lunar can at least understand the risks can be worth it). Implementation counts for a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:38:36-08:00","id":397914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397832#post397832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really care for the notion that your native splat power is also the source of your epic weakness. I mean sure, it logically makes sense, I just don't care for tying negative mechanics to a power you want to incentivize use of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's kind of the point of the great curse all around though, the Primordials took a look at what each host of exalted did best and said &quot;we can't take your power away from you but we will leave you with this curse that will forever punish you for exercising that power&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T12:55:16-08:00","id":397924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/397162-speculation-on-the-lunar-curse?p=397525#post397525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we please not? There's a time and a place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough; that said, no one here (excepting maybe the playtesters) knows what a <i>Solar</i> Limit Break looks like either. When John said &quot;&quot;Lunar Limit Breaks are undetermined, but are likely to change from what they were,&quot; it's very likely worth considering that they are still going to be an epic hero release valve, as someone suggested earlier, just not &quot;mostly identical to Solar Limit Break in expression, but with lesser duration and oh yeah, you're guaranteed to get at least three points of Limit each month from the full moon.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}